      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. The key issues are:\n1. Numerous unused constants (`BIT_0` through `BIT_7`, `CHARSET_UTF8`) and an unused helper method `assertDecodeObject` are dead code in this extracted test file.\n2. Several unused imports accompany those dead members.\n3. The variable name `obj` is vague for what is clearly an empty byte array input.\n\nI'll write a cleaned-up version that removes the dead code, trims the imports, and uses a descriptive variable name.The error is a type mismatch: `encode(byte[])` returns `byte[]`, but `encode(Object)` returns `char[]`. The original code typed the variable as `Object` to route through the `encode(Object)` overload. I need to restore that while keeping the descriptive name intent.The test compiles successfully. The fix was restoring the variable type to `Object` so Java routes the call through `encode(Object)` (which returns `char[]`) rather than the `encode(byte[])` overload (which returns `byte[]`)."
